{"author":{"id":"fd8b9fbee3ca9e1e8bc93ac1e52482b167d597d9903cceb294967fa0f6114e08"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786489080,"nonce":"JZs0rF6nV8qMcnTdM5AJQ7r+CHE=","message":"Reproduced, localized, and attributed: this is a defect in Gunlok itself, not our overlay ordering.\n\n**The A/B the issue asked for says it is not ours.** level02, camera settled at the same five\nvalues and 178 actors under both, paused: the HUD region is identical under GKPLUS_RENDERER=d3d8\nand GKPLUS_RENDERER=vulkan. Same empty meter troughs, same portrait on top.\n\n**And it reproduces with GkPlus not in the process at all.** d3d8.dll renamed aside (version\nstamp back to the stock \"v1.3 DX8\"), Single Player -\u003e Training Level -\u003e Area 1, driven by mouse\nclicks since there is no REPL: same empty troughs, same empty item slots.\n\n**Which draw is which**, from `render.frame_draws` on a paused level02 frame under d3d8. Three\nconsecutive draws, all sampling `units\\plates 2 1024.rim`:\n\n```\nidx  prims  fvf    blend ztest zwrite  viewport MinZ..MaxZ\n 65     12  0x1c4   off    on     on   0.1000 .. 1.0000\n 66      2  0x112   off    on     on   0.0299 .. 0.0399\n 67      2  0x112   off    on     on   0.0299 .. 0.0399\n```\n\n`render.ref_hide = [66, 67]` makes the two character panels vanish and reveals, underneath,\nbright green filled meter bars and the item icons in their slots. `ref_hide = [65, 67]` removes\nthose too. So draw 65 is the meters and icons, 66/67 are the panel backgrounds, and the panel is\nopaque and z-writing over them.\n\n**The mechanism** (ghidra-analyst against gl.exe). The engine layers HUD content by giving each\ncamera its own viewport depth slice - `InitRenderCameras` @ 0x004af4d0 carves them: Camera_Menu2D\n0.00-0.02, Camera_Text 0.02-0.04, Camera_Hud 0.03-0.04, Camera_World 0.10-1.00. The printed\n0.0299/0.0399 are %.4f-truncated 0.03f/0.04f.\n\nThe panel plates are retained render-queue items and all 11 submit sites in HudItem_DrawByKind\n@ 0x0055fbd0 (the function the DB called `DrawHud`) pass Camera_Hud. The meters and icons never\ngo through the queue - they are appended to a shared immediate-mode vertex batch by\nHud2D_DrawQuad @ 0x005695c0 with an explicitly authored **z = 0.03f**, i.e. exactly Camera_Hud\nMinZ, the front of the HUD slice. That is unambiguous intent: the meters belong in front of the\nplates.\n\nThe bug is frame ordering in RunInGameFrame:\n\n```\n0046e8c1  CALL RenderHudItems     ; makes Camera_Hud current (viewport 0.03..0.04)\n0046e8ca  CALL DrawOrderMenu      ; makes Camera_World current again (0.1..1.0)   \u003c-- the culprit\n0046e8cf  CALL Hud2D_FlushBatch   ; draws the meter quads under the WORLD viewport\n...       RenderQueue_Flush       ; draws the panel plates with Camera_Hud\n```\n\nvulkan_renderer_notes.md 4.45 already measured, with a probe against the real D3D8, that D3D does\nnot run the viewport transform over a pre-transformed vertex - it clamps: depth = clamp(z, MinZ,\nMaxZ). So the authored 0.03 is clamped **up** to 0.1 and lands behind the whole HUD slice. 4.45\neven describes this bar in passing and read the panel covering it as correct reference behaviour.\n\nNothing in HudItem_DrawByKind is wrong: in its own source order it submits the plate before it\nemits the meter quads.\n\nNext: a HudFixSystem in GkPlus that makes Camera_Hud current before the batch flush, then\ngame_defects_notes.md.","files":null}]}